 "kind": "A diagnostic after the fact, on trained weights, with no training and no pass mark. It extends unit_density.json, which measured one pair of the plain test bed at 3e-4 and said that nothing was measured at full size.",
 "why": "unit_density.json found the Transformer's units as dense as the stack's cells, and the roadmap took a sparser code off the list on that. Both models have since moved to higher peak rates (1.2e-3 and 2.4e-3 on the test bed, 6e-4 and 1.2e-3 at full size), and the roadmap's seventh bet, cells that keep themselves in the range where they still learn, had no measurement of how many cells are out of it.",
 "measure": "experiments/cell_activity.py on stacks, as 16 unbroken streams after 1,024 lead bytes: the share of a level's cells that fire at a byte, the share whose largest counts add up to nine tenths of the level's spikes at a byte, and the cells that never fire. experiments/unit_density.py on Transformers, on the second half of every window: the share of a block's units whose gate's drive is above zero, and the share whose largest outputs add up to nine tenths of what the block's units pass on. Both nine-tenths measures are taken before the output synapses. Averaged weights, the first validation bytes: 65,536 for the test bed and the Transformers, 32,768 for the full-size stacks; windows of 256 bytes for the test bed's Transformers and 512 for the full size's. Each entry gives the median over the levels or blocks, then the lowest and the highest. A cell's resting charge and the norm of its input synapses are read from the checkpoint. Full size: the 24,000-update pilots of full_size_rate_pilot.json and full_size_lifted_ceiling_pilot.json, fs-noise6 of full_size_unit_screen.json, and the headline pair (l2048-word-st and tf2048, 90,000 updates). Test bed: the two seeds of learning_rate_with_data.json at five rates, and the laptop's seed 20003 at 1.2e-3 at 6,000 and 24,000 updates (rd-base-6k-s3, rd-base-24k-s3). On the CPU. For plain cells the tool also counts the cells and bytes by the cell's charge in thresholds, after its rest is taken off; that count was taken for the laptop's seed.",
 "seen_before_recording": "All of it: the measurement was read as it came in, and the nine-tenths measure for cells was added to experiments/cell_activity.py after the first pass showed the firing shares.",
